Custom exceptions are the exceptions which are defined by user as per the requirements for a project. These are the exceptions for the scenarios
which are not pre-defined.
To create a custom exception, we have to follow certain rules.
1) Create a class, the name of the class should be same of the exception name.
2) This class can extend the Exception super class to create a checked exception or it can extend RuntimeException class to create an unchecked
exception.
3) To invoke this exception we have to create an object of this custom exception class and use the 'throw' keyword to throw this object. 
4) This will invoke the custom exception. We can pair this with condtional statements so that the exception invokes upon certian condition.
